format 1
adapter feed 1
npc: npc-mina

post ft-mina-chest-daily
kind: celebrate
trigger: chest_opened
chip: quests
condition: {"period":"daily"}

text:
    You opened the daily chest. A small reward, and a gentle reminder that small steps count.

post ft-mina-chest-weekly
kind: celebrate
trigger: chest_opened
chip: quests
condition: {"period":"weekly"}

text:
    The weekly chest is open. A whole week of quests, done at your own pace. That takes care and patience.

post ft-mina-first-lesson
kind: celebrate
trigger: first_lesson
chip: lesson

text:
    Your first lesson is done: “{lesson}”. Well done. It is normal to feel a little unsure at the start, and you did it anyway.

post ft-mina-lesson-dose-and-time-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"dose-and-time"}

text:
    “{lesson}” done. A big dose in a short time and a small one spread out are very different things.

post ft-mina-lesson-dose-and-time-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"dose-and-time"}

text:
    You finished “{lesson}”. How fast a dose arrives matters as much as how big it is.

post ft-mina-lesson-dose-and-time-3
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"dose-and-time","perfect":true}

text:
    Perfect on “{lesson}”. Size and speed, both kept straight.

post ft-mina-lesson-radiation-and-cells-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"radiation-and-cells"}

text:
    “{lesson}” done. Radiation can damage a cell, and cells are extremely good at repairing it. Both halves are true.

post ft-mina-lesson-radiation-and-cells-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"radiation-and-cells"}

text:
    You finished “{lesson}”. That is the worry and the reassurance, side by side.

post ft-mina-lesson-radiation-and-cells-3
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"radiation-and-cells","perfect":true}

text:
    Perfect on “{lesson}”. You kept both halves in mind. That is not easy.

post ft-mina-lesson-risk-in-perspective-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"risk-in-perspective"}

text:
    “{lesson}” done. Size, speed and comparison turn a scary number into something you can judge.

post ft-mina-lesson-risk-in-perspective-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"risk-in-perspective"}

text:
    You finished “{lesson}”. You can read a frightening headline calmly now.

post ft-mina-lesson-risk-in-perspective-3
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"risk-in-perspective","perfect":true}

text:
    Perfect on “{lesson}”. A calm head and the right questions.

post ft-mina-lesson-the-dose-scale-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"the-dose-scale"}

text:
    “{lesson}” done. A little radiation every day is normal, and now you can count it in millisieverts.

post ft-mina-lesson-the-dose-scale-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"the-dose-scale"}

text:
    Another lesson on the scale, “{lesson}”. You can put an ordinary year, a scan and an illness in order now.

post ft-mina-lesson-the-dose-scale-3
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"the-dose-scale","perfect":true}

text:
    Perfect on “{lesson}”. Careful counting, and not one number mixed up.

post ft-mina-lesson-time-distance-shielding-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"time-distance-shielding"}

text:
    “{lesson}” done. Less time, more distance, and something in between. Three ways anyone can lower a dose.

post ft-mina-lesson-time-distance-shielding-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"time-distance-shielding"}

text:
    You finished “{lesson}”. A lead apron at the dentist is shielding. You will notice it now.

post ft-mina-lesson-time-distance-shielding-3
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body","lessonId":"time-distance-shielding","perfect":true}

text:
    Perfect on “{lesson}”. You picked the right way every time.

post ft-mina-quests
kind: celebrate
trigger: daily_quests_done
chip: quests

text:
    Every daily quest is claimed. You did well today. Take a breath, then open your chest.

post ft-mina-rank-passed
kind: celebrate
trigger: rank_change
chip: ranks
condition: {"direction":"passed"}

text:
    You passed {rival} in the weekly ranking. Lovely. And remember, it is fine to go at your own speed.

post ft-mina-checkpoint-radiation-and-the-body
kind: milestone
trigger: checkpoint_pass
chip: unit
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body"}
reactors: npc-ray

text:
    The {unit} checkpoint is passed. You took it steadily, and it shows.

post ft-mina-testout-radiation-and-the-body
kind: milestone
trigger: testout_pass
chip: unit
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body"}
reactors: npc-ray

text:
    You tested out of “{unit}”. You already understood it. That's a good place to start from.

post ft-mina-unit-radiation-and-the-body-2
kind: milestone
trigger: unit_complete
chip: unit
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-and-the-body"}
reactors: npc-ray

text:
    You finished “{unit}”. You can say how big a dose is, how cells cope, and how to lower a dose. A calm, solid understanding.

post ft-mina-unit-radiation-meets-matter-1
kind: milestone
trigger: unit_complete
chip: unit
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter"}
reactors: npc-ray

text:
    Someone just finished “{unit}” with Ray. They know what radiation does to things. Now we talk about the body, calmly and slowly. That part is mine.

post ft-mina-comeback-14
kind: nudge
trigger: comeback
condition: {"minDays":14}

text:
    Hello again, {name}. Life gets busy, and that is okay. One calm lesson is plenty to start.

post ft-mina-comeback-3
kind: nudge
trigger: comeback
condition: {"minDays":3}

text:
    Welcome back, {name}. No pressure at all. Pick up wherever feels comfortable.

post ft-mina-rank-passed-by
kind: nudge
trigger: rank_change
chip: ranks
condition: {"direction":"passed_by"}

text:
    {rival} passed you in the weekly ranking. That is okay. A ranking is only a snapshot. One lesson at a time.
